laurel 2973: SPMI: a CPU that waits for the transaction lock takes interrupts

sp_xfer_take spun with interrupts off for up to 5 ms; a holder keeps the lock up to 1 ms per transaction. A stackshot waits at most 100 ms now (post/9007), 12.5 ms before: a waiter here was the only one of our paths with a long interrupt-off wait [V code: the other ml_set_interrupts_enabled(FALSE) of our code is in kprintf]. Not shown to be why CPU 5 was late in boot 11 [U]. Interrupts stay off while the lock is held, as before. No new line: no feature to turn off.

diff --git a/bsd/dev/sweet_spmi.c b/bsd/dev/sweet_spmi.c
--- a/bsd/dev/sweet_spmi.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/sweet_spmi.c
@@ -119,7 +119,10 @@
 			ml_set_interrupts_enabled(*istate);
 			return -1;
 		}
+		/* laurel 2973: a waiter takes interrupts while it waits (up to SP_LOCK_WAIT_US). Off only while it may hold the lock. */
+		(void)ml_set_interrupts_enabled(*istate);
 		__asm__ volatile("yield");
+		(void)ml_set_interrupts_enabled(FALSE);
 	}
 }
 
